# Architectural Design & Specification Report: `crates/flightreader-export`

**Author**: Explorer M1-1 (OpenFlightReader Phase 3 Milestone M1)  
**Date**: 2026-10-28  
**Scope**: Core Data Models (`src/model.rs`), Stateful Zero-Order Hold Aggregator (`src/aggregator.rs`), Time-Window & Landmark-Pinning Filtering Engine (`src/filter.rs`), Crate Architecture & Dependencies (`Cargo.toml`).  
**Working Directory**: `/home/prem/Projects/Flightreader/.agents/teamwork/teamwork_preview_explorer_m1_1/`  
**Integrity Mode**: Read-Only Architecture & Design Specification  

---

## 1. Executive Summary & Architectural Overview

Phase 3 of OpenFlightReader delivers the export, visualization, and application layer on top of `flightreader-core`. The core engine (`flightreader-core`, delivered in Phases 1 and 2) produces asynchronous, strongly-typed telemetry records:
- **OSD Telemetry (Record Type 1)**: Primary navigation cadence (~10 Hz).
- **Home Point Telemetry (Record Type 2)**: Navigation reference & blackbox index (~1 Hz).
- **Gimbal Telemetry (Record Type 3)**: Attitude cadence (~10–20 Hz).
- **RC Sticks (Record Type 4)**: Pilot control inputs (~10–20 Hz).
- **Battery Suite (Record Types 6, 7, 8, 22, 50)**: Diagnostic cadence (~1–2 Hz).
- **Blackbox `.DAT` Frames (Payloads 0x01, 0x12, 0x0A)**: High-frequency sensor samples (50–200 Hz).

Because each sensor stream reports at divergent frequencies and non-coincident timestamps, exporting tabular (CSV) or geospatial (KML, GPX, GeoJSON) flight logs cannot write one row per raw record envelope. Doing so would produce sparse, incomplete rows where Battery rows lack coordinates and OSD rows lack battery metrics.

`crates/flightreader-export` provides the foundational aggregation and filtering pipeline that converts these divergent streams into a clean, synchronized, 10 Hz monotonic time-series (`FlightDataset`) ready for downstream export and visualization.

```
                  Raw Binary Flight Log (.txt / .DAT)
                                  │
                                  ▼
                      crates/flightreader-core
               (RecordEnvelopeIterator / DatFrameIterator)
                                  │
                                  ▼
                     crates/flightreader-export
         ┌────────────────────────┴────────────────────────┐
         ▼                                                 ▼
TelemetryAggregator                                  FilterPipeline
- Zero-Order Hold (ZOH) forward-fill                 - Time window (--start, --end)
- Master clock timestamp calculation                 - Rate decimation (--rate <HZ>)
- Ground increment + airborne sync                   - Critical landmark event pinning
- Geodetic MSL (EGM2008) & AGL elevations             (Takeoff, Landing, Mode, RTH, Extrema)
         │                                                 │
         └────────────────────────┬────────────────────────┘
                                  ▼
                            FlightDataset
                     (Metadata, Points, Events)
                                  │
              ┌───────────────────┼───────────────────┐
              ▼                   ▼                   ▼
          CSV Export          KML Export          GPX Export
          (RFC 4180)          (OGC 2.2)         (TopoGrafix 1.1)
```

---

## 2. Crate Setup & Dependencies (`crates/flightreader-export/Cargo.toml`)

### 2.1 `#![deny(unsafe_code)]` Compliance
Per project requirements and ADR-001, `crates/flightreader-export` must strictly enforce `#![deny(unsafe_code)]` at the root of `src/lib.rs`. Zero `unsafe` blocks are permitted. All memory operations use safe Rust slices, iterators, and checked arithmetic.

### 2.2 Dependency Catalog
The crate dependencies are strictly scoped to pure-Rust, memory-safe libraries:

```toml
[package]
name = "flightreader-export"
version = "0.1.0"
edition = "2021"
authors = ["OpenFlightReader Contributors"]
license = "MIT OR Apache-2.0"
description = "High-performance geospatial, tabular, and time-series telemetry export engine for OpenFlightReader."

[dependencies]
# Core binary parsing, cryptographic de-scrambling, and EGM2008 geodesy
flightreader-core = { path = "../flightreader-core" }

# Strongly-typed error definition
thiserror = "2.0"

# Serialization and data interchange
serde = { version = "1.0", features = ["derive"] }
serde_json = "1.0"

# Strict UTC and ISO 8601 timestamp parsing and formatting
chrono = { version = "0.4", default-features = false, features = ["std", "clock"] }

# Binary primitives (for reading details block offsets)
byteorder = "1.5"

# Streaming XML generation (pure-Rust, safe)
quick-xml = { version = "0.37", features = ["serialize"] }

[dev-dependencies]
tempfile = "3.17"
```

### 2.3 Workspace Integration
The root `/home/prem/Projects/Flightreader/Cargo.toml` workspace definition must be updated to include `crates/flightreader-export`:
```toml
[workspace]
members = [
    "crates/flightreader-core",
    "crates/flightreader-export",
]
resolver = "2"
```

---

## 3. Data Model Architecture (`src/model.rs`)

The data model provides the unified representation consumed by all downstream exporters (CSV, KML, GPX, GeoJSON, and local server state).

### 3.1 `TelemetryPoint`
A single synchronized time-series point capturing the aircraft's physical state at a discrete 10 Hz instant:

```rust
use serde::{Deserialize, Serialize};

/// A synchronized, multi-sensor flight telemetry point at a discrete instant.
#[derive(Debug, Clone, PartialEq, Serialize, Deserialize)]
pub struct TelemetryPoint {
    /// Monotonically increasing sequential index of this point in the dataset (0-based).
    pub index: usize,
    /// Absolute UTC Unix timestamp in milliseconds.
    pub timestamp_utc_ms: i64,
    /// ISO 8601 formatted UTC timestamp string (e.g. "2026-10-27T14:32:00.100Z").
    pub timestamp_iso8601: String,
    /// Cumulative elapsed duration in seconds since logging began (monotonically increasing).
    pub elapsed_s: f64,
    /// Official DJI airborne flight timer in seconds (0.0 during pre-takeoff ground idling).
    pub fly_time_s: f64,

    // --- Spatial Position & Vertical Datums ---
    /// WGS84 Geodetic Latitude in decimal degrees (-90.0 to +90.0).
    pub latitude: f64,
    /// WGS84 Geodetic Longitude in decimal degrees (-180.0 to +180.0).
    pub longitude: f64,
    /// Orthometric altitude above Mean Sea Level (MSL) in meters (via EGM2008 / Home datum).
    pub altitude_msl: f64,
    /// Relative altitude Above Ground Level (AGL) in meters relative to takeoff point.
    pub altitude_agl: f64,
    /// Raw barometric relative height from OSD in meters.
    pub altitude_baro: f64,
    /// Ultrasonic / optical flow ground clearance in meters (if sensor active).
    pub vps_height_m: Option<f64>,

    // --- Kinematics & Velocities (NED Frame) ---
    /// Horizontal ground speed in m/s (sqrt(vel_n^2 + vel_e^2)).
    pub ground_speed_mps: f64,
    /// 3D total speed magnitude in m/s (sqrt(vel_n^2 + vel_e^2 + vel_d^2)).
    pub speed_3d_mps: f64,
    /// Climb rate in m/s (-vel_d, positive = ascending).
    pub climb_rate_mps: f64,
    /// Velocity along North axis in m/s (NED frame).
    pub vel_n: f64,
    /// Velocity along East axis in m/s (NED frame).
    pub vel_e: f64,
    /// Velocity along Down axis in m/s (NED frame).
    pub vel_d: f64,
    /// Ground track course bearing in degrees clockwise from True North (0.0 to 360.0).
    pub course_deg: f64,

    // --- Aircraft Attitude (Euler Angles) ---
    /// Aircraft pitch angle in degrees (-90.0 nose down to +90.0 nose up).
    pub pitch_deg: f64,
    /// Aircraft roll angle in degrees (-180.0 to +180.0, positive = right wing down).
    pub roll_deg: f64,
    /// Aircraft yaw angle in degrees (-180.0 to +180.0).
    pub yaw_deg: f64,
    /// Normalized compass heading in degrees (0.0 to 360.0, 0.0 = True North).
    pub heading_deg: f64,

    // --- Camera Gimbal ---
    /// Gimbal pitch angle in degrees (-90.0 nadir to +30.0 up).
    pub gimbal_pitch_deg: f64,
    /// Gimbal roll leveling angle in degrees.
    pub gimbal_roll_deg: f64,
    /// Gimbal yaw angle in degrees relative to aircraft nose.
    pub gimbal_yaw_deg: f64,
    /// Stabilization operational mode ("Free", "Fpv", "Follow", "Unknown").
    pub gimbal_mode: String,

    // --- Remote Controller Inputs ---
    /// Normalized aileron (roll) stick input (-1.0 left to +1.0 right).
    pub rc_aileron: f64,
    /// Normalized elevator (pitch) stick input (-1.0 backward to +1.0 forward).
    pub rc_elevator: f64,
    /// Normalized throttle (climb) stick input (-1.0 descend to +1.0 ascend).
    pub rc_throttle: f64,
    /// Normalized rudder (yaw) stick input (-1.0 turn left to +1.0 turn right).
    pub rc_rudder: f64,
    /// Flight mode switch position label ("P", "S", "A", etc.).
    pub rc_mode_switch: String,
    /// Radio link signal quality / RSSI percentage (0 to 100%).
    pub rc_signal_quality: u8,

    // --- Battery Health & Metrics ---
    /// State of Charge (SOC) percentage (0 to 100%).
    pub battery_pct: u8,
    /// Pack terminal voltage in millivolts.
    pub battery_voltage_mv: u32,
    /// Pack temperature in degrees Celsius.
    pub battery_temp_c: f64,
    /// Instantaneous current draw in Amperes (positive = discharging).
    pub battery_current_a: Option<f64>,
    /// Individual cell voltages in millivolts (cells 1..=14).
    pub cell_voltages_mv: Vec<u16>,
    /// Voltage delta between highest and lowest active cell in millivolts.
    pub cell_deviation_mv: u16,

    // --- Navigation & Safety Status ---
    /// Count of locked GNSS satellites.
    pub gps_satellites: u8,
    /// GNSS signal health level (0 to 5 bars).
    pub gps_level: u8,
    /// Flight controller flight mode ("P-GPS", "Sport", "Atti", "Auto-RTH", etc.).
    pub flight_mode: String,
    /// Ground contact state ("Airborne", "OnGround", "Landing").
    pub ground_state: String,
    /// Whether propulsion motors are armed and running.
    pub is_motor_on: bool,
    /// Whether Return-To-Home failsafe is currently active.
    pub is_failsafe_active: bool,
    /// Operational pilot warning message (if active).
    pub app_warning: Option<String>,
    /// Operational status tip (if active).
    pub app_tip: Option<String>,
}
```

### 3.2 `FlightEvent` & `FlightEventType`
Captures discrete occurrences and safety-critical state transitions during the mission:

```rust
/// The semantic category of a flight milestone or safety event.
#[derive(Debug, Clone, PartialEq, Eq, Hash, Serialize, Deserialize)]
pub enum FlightEventType {
    /// Propulsion motors spun up and aircraft departed ground surface.
    Takeoff,
    /// Aircraft touched down and propulsion motors were disarmed.
    Landing,
    /// Home Point coordinate calibration was locked or updated.
    HomeRecorded,
    /// Flight controller transitioned between flight modes.
    FlightModeChange { from: String, to: String },
    /// Return-To-Home failsafe was engaged (low battery, signal loss, or pilot command).
    RthTriggered,
    /// Ground station application emitted a safety alert or operational warning.
    Warning { message: String },
    /// Maximum altitude point attained during sortie.
    MaxAltitude,
    /// Maximum ground speed point attained during sortie.
    MaxSpeed,
    /// Custom vendor or user event marker.
    Custom(String),
}

/// A flight event record pinned to an exact timestamp and optional coordinate.
#[derive(Debug, Clone, PartialEq, Serialize, Deserialize)]
pub struct FlightEvent {
    /// UTC Unix epoch timestamp in milliseconds when event transpired.
    pub timestamp_utc_ms: i64,
    /// Elapsed seconds since log start.
    pub elapsed_s: f64,
    /// Event classification.
    pub event_type: FlightEventType,
    /// Human-readable description of event.
    pub description: String,
    /// Latitude where event occurred.
    pub latitude: Option<f64>,
    /// Longitude where event occurred.
    pub longitude: Option<f64>,
    /// Altitude MSL in meters where event occurred.
    pub altitude_msl: Option<f64>,
}
```

### 3.3 `FlightMetadata`
Captures session summary statistics and aircraft hardware identities:

```rust
/// Comprehensive overview metadata for a parsed flight log.
#[derive(Debug, Clone, PartialEq, Serialize, Deserialize)]
pub struct FlightMetadata {
    /// Log format identifier (e.g. "DJI_TXT_V12", "DJI_DAT").
